From 57bb81adc08ee36e0ab8e84129ed9d9d2887ec45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): preserve Codex quota benches and rotate past
 readmitted rows [daveey]

Reproduce with the real three-row fill-first pool and HTTP-only usage stubs: an open short window erased a six-day quota wall, hid healthy B and produced the non-retryable no-selected-entry error. Require evidence for the persisted reset window and do not reuse positive evidence from an older failure generation. Preserve quota when adopting a singleton token pair. Reapply a just-marked account failure and exclude its row before resync/probes, preserving stale terminal-token generation safety. Log early bench lifts at INFO.

Proof: three regression tests RED on 89a90ff35bed; five new tests GREEN; 412 tests in 47 pool/auth/model-routing files passed; all 20 scripts/check gates passed against the implementation base. Further consumer/mutation checks and compatibility-pin audit remain before publication.
